# ── Secrets — never commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*.ppk
credentials.json
service-account*.json
.npmrc
.netrc

# ── Runtime state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Snapshots (holder velocity), deployer cache, and the alert dedupe log.
# Machine-local and regenerable — keep it out of git.
.state/
**/.state/

# ── Generated output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aegis writes a new note every scan, so this folder grows continuously and
# is fully regenerable. Tracking it would add thousands of churning files to
# every push and gives the Render deploy nothing.
# Delete the line below if you want your notes backed up in git.
Memecoin/Crypto finder/Signals/

# Obsidian per-machine UI state (keep the vault config, drop the workspace).
# Needs the ** prefix: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the repo
# root, so a bare `.obsidian/workspace.json` would miss the nested vault.
**/.obsidian/workspace.json
**/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
package-lock.json

# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Personal notes — may contain keys pasted while configuring
00 To Do List.md
*To Do List.md

# ── Wallet recovery material — NEVER commit ─────────────────────────────
# "Axiom Recovery.txt" was sitting untracked in the repo root holding a
# 12-word BIP39 seed phrase. A seed phrase in a git history is game over:
# history is permanent, bots scrape pushes within minutes, and rotating a
# compromised wallet means moving every asset out of it first.
# Keep recovery material in a password manager, never in the working tree.
*Recovery*.txt
*recovery*.txt
*seed*.txt
*mnemonic*
*.wallet
wallet.json
keypair*.json

# Runtime logs
*.log

# Stray files from malformed shell args
*gmail.com*
*.log.*
loop.log*
